tor choice changes nothing and a parenthetical note supplies no part. A part is its file, or its file and test with a class retained and a parametrized case removed. A file part binds only to a file-level declaration and a test part only to that test's declaration, so a test part in a file read at file level is two differences. A test's declaration repeating its file's declaration is still a declaration, so its cell names that test as well. A part outside the tests root is outside the rule. A tests root of `.` holds every part in the repository. An uncovered part is reported as evidence without a tag, and an unreferenced declaration as tag without evidence; each names the test case and node. A file refused as unreadable adds no finding here, and an absent tests root or test-case registry makes the check vacuous. Findings warn without strict checking and error under strict checking; they gate from DevStg-Impl and remain warnings below that rung, including in a newly created project. The contract covers live test cases, their Evidence cells, declarations in files under the declared tests root, and supported workflows; evidence outside that root, a parenthetical note, and a file refused as unreadable are outside it.\""," rationale = \"A declaration can be live yet omit a case's evidence, or name a case whose evidence does not reach it, leaving the trace between test case and test file inconsistent without an attributable finding. The existing cell reader and declaration reader already define the shared terms, so this contract compares their results rather than creating another interpretation.\""," test_refs = \"TC-410; TC-411; TC-412\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-006\""," phase = 6"," "]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-997\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1617,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1617,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Each evidence without a tag and tag wit